commits.message:
refactor(logger): drop source maps; remove vault-manager swc workaround

@growi/logger is a small, private utility whose own stack frames are noise relative to the caller's, so it does not need source maps. Emitting external .map files also tripped @swc-node's ESM loader with spurious 'failed to read input source map' errors in growi-vault-manager (its only @swc-node/register consumer of the logger). Set sourcemap: false in the logger build so no .map files or sourceMappingURL comments are emitted and the loader has nothing to resolve. With the noise gone at the root, drop growi-vault-manager's SWCRC=true + .swcrc workaround: @swc-node/register derives the decorator/metadata transform from tsconfig (experimentalDecorators/emitDecoratorMetadata). Verified: logger import emits zero source-map errors, 181 vault-manager unit tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
